# Coding standards

- TypeScript **strict**. No `any` at money or auth boundaries.
- **Zod** at every system boundary (forms, Server Actions, API, AI structured output).
- Mutations via Server Actions; API routes only when needed.
- No business logic in React components. No DB queries in presentation.
- Money math lives in `lib/money` as pure functions with tests.
- Prefer small milestones. Do not implement the whole company in one PR.
- Do not add dependencies without a clear reason.
- Do not use fake calculations in production paths.
- Do not hardcode user-specific financial assumptions.
- Follow existing shadcn / Tailwind patterns once a design direction is locked (`docs/UX-AND-BRAND.md`).
- Centralize visual values as design tokens — do not scatter magic colors per component after the design system exists.
